IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `pip-nouns`
IMPORT `pip-dates`

-- PART 1 -- GENERAL: regulation 1 (citation and commencement) and regulation 2
-- (interpretation).
--
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Nobody's point of view is taken here.
--
-- The lines of the text this module rests on are quoted with `-- src:N |` and each rule
-- carries an @ref whose locator names the same lines (python3 -I srcrefs.py check --refs).

§ `Title block and regulation 1: citation and commencement`

-- The title block says when the Regulations were made. It is a date, so it is data.
-- src:4 | Made 25th February 2013
@ref Made 25th February 2013 (src:4)
`the date these Regulations were made` MEANS YearMonthDay 2013 2 25

-- reg 1(1) gives the short title. A pure citation: it decides nothing, so it is carried
-- as a string and nothing calls it.
-- src:11 | (1) These Regulations may be cited as the Social Security (Personal Independence Payment) Regulations 2013.
@ref reg 1(1) (src:11)
`the short title of these Regulations` MEANS
    "Social Security (Personal Independence Payment) Regulations 2013"

-- reg 1(2): the Regulations come into force, in relation to one case, on the day Part 4
-- of the Act (the Welfare Reform Act 2012) comes into force in relation to that case. That
-- day is fixed by the Act and its commencement orders, which are not among the inputs, so it
-- is taken as an input.
-- out of text: Welfare Reform Act 2012 Part 4 and the orders bringing it into force
-- src:12 | (2) These Regulations come into force in relation to a particular case on the day on which Part 4 of the Act comes into force in relation to that case .
@ref reg 1(2) (src:12)
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
      `the day Part 4 of the Act comes into force for the case` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 1(2): these Regulations are in force in the case on` `the day` `, Part 4 of the Act coming into force in the case on` `the day Part 4 of the Act comes into force for the case` MEANS
    `the day` AT LEAST `the day Part 4 of the Act comes into force for the case`

§ `Regulation 2: interpretation`

-- "aid or appliance" means any device which improves, provides or replaces C's impaired
-- physical or mental function; and includes a prosthesis. The two limbs are cumulative in
-- the grammar of the text only in the sense that (b) adds a case: a prosthesis is an aid or
-- appliance whether or not it also improves, provides or replaces a function.
-- src:18 | “aid or appliance”—
-- src:19 | (a) means any device which improves, provides or replaces C's impaired physical or mental function; and
-- src:20 | (b) includes a prosthesis;
@ref reg 2 "aid or appliance" (src:18-20)
GIVEN `the device improves C's impaired physical or mental function` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the device provides C's impaired physical or mental function` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the device replaces C's impaired physical or mental function` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the device is a prosthesis` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 2: a device is an aid or appliance` MEANS
        (   `the device improves C's impaired physical or mental function`
         OR `the device provides C's impaired physical or mental function`
         OR `the device replaces C's impaired physical or mental function`)
     OR `the device is a prosthesis`

-- "assessment" means the assessment referred to in regulation 4. Nothing to compute here:
-- regulation 4 (pip-part2-assessment.l4) is where the assessment is encoded.
-- src:21 | “assessment” means the assessment referred to in regulation 4;
@ref reg 2 "assessment" (src:21)
`reg 2: the assessment is the assessment referred to in regulation 4` MEANS
    "“assessment” means the assessment referred to in regulation 4;"

-- "C" means a person who has made a claim for or, as the case may be, is entitled to
-- personal independence payment.
-- src:22 | “C” means a person who has made a claim for or, as the case may be, is entitled to personal independence payment;
@ref reg 2 "C" (src:22)
GIVEN `the person has made a claim for personal independence payment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is entitled to personal independence payment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 2: a person is C` MEANS
       `the person has made a claim for personal independence payment`
    OR `the person is entitled to personal independence payment`

-- "component" means the daily living component or, as the case may be, the mobility
-- component of personal independence payment: the noun `a component of personal
-- independence payment` of pip-nouns.l4.
-- src:24 | “component” means the daily living component or, as the case may be, the mobility component of personal independence payment;
@ref reg 2 "component" (src:24)
GIVEN c IS A `a component of personal independence payment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 2: this is a component of personal independence payment` c MEANS
    c EQUALS `the daily living component` OR c EQUALS `the mobility component`

-- "descriptor" means a descriptor in column 2 of the tables in Parts 2 and 3 of Schedule 1:
-- a row of pip-sch1-daily-living-table.l4 or pip-sch1-mobility-table.l4, whose words are
-- in its `its words` field.
-- src:25 | “descriptor” means a descriptor in column 2 of the tables in Parts 2 and 3 of Schedule 1;
@ref reg 2 "descriptor" (src:25)
`reg 2: a descriptor is a descriptor in column 2 of the tables in Parts 2 and 3 of Schedule 1` MEANS
    "“descriptor” means a descriptor in column 2 of the tables in Parts 2 and 3 of Schedule 1;"

-- "medical treatment" means medical, surgical or rehabilitative treatment (including any
-- course or diet or other regimen).
DECLARE `a kind of health intervention` IS ONE OF
    `medical treatment in the ordinary sense`
    `surgical treatment`
    `rehabilitative treatment`
    `a course or diet or other regimen`
    `some other intervention`

-- src:27 | “medical treatment” means medical, surgical or rehabilitative treatment (including any course or diet or other regimen), and references to a person receiving or submitting to medical treatment are to be construed accordingly;
@ref reg 2 "medical treatment" (src:27)
GIVEN i IS A `a kind of health intervention`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 2: an intervention is medical treatment` i MEANS
    NOT (i EQUALS `some other intervention`)

-- "previous award" means an award of either or both components to which C has ceased to be
-- entitled.
-- src:29 | “previous award” means an award of either or both components to which C has ceased to be entitled;
@ref reg 2 "previous award" (src:29)
GIVEN `the award is of either or both components` IS A BOOLEAN
      `C has ceased to be entitled to the award` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 2: an award is a previous award` MEANS
        `the award is of either or both components`
    AND `C has ceased to be entitled to the award`

-- "the residence change date", in relation to a person, means the date on which the person
-- becomes permanently resident in Scotland, whether or not the Secretary of State is notified of
-- the move and whether or not any such notification takes place before or after the person moves.
-- So the date does not depend on notification; the rule takes the date of the move and nothing else.
-- src:30 | “the residence change date”, in relation to a person, means the date on which the person becomes permanently resident in Scotland (whether or not the Secretary of State is notified of the move and whether or not any such notification takes place before or after the person moves to Scotland);
@ref reg 2 "the residence change date" (src:30)
GIVEN `the date on which the person becomes permanently resident in Scotland` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 2: the residence change date` MEANS
    `the date on which the person becomes permanently resident in Scotland`

-- "revised" and "superseded" take their meaning from sections 9 and 10 of the Social
-- Security Act 1998 (the 1998 Act), which is not among the inputs.
-- out of text: Social Security Act 1998 ss 9, 10
DECLARE `how a decision on an award is changed` IS ONE OF
    `revision under section 9 of the 1998 Act`
    `supersession under section 10 of the 1998 Act`
    `a change that is neither a revision nor a supersession`

-- src:31 | “revised” means revised under section 9 of the 1998 Act, and “revision” is to be construed accordingly;
@ref reg 2 "revised" (src:31)
GIVEN h IS A `how a decision on an award is changed`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 2: a decision on an award is revised` h MEANS
    h EQUALS `revision under section 9 of the 1998 Act`

-- src:34 | “superseded” means superseded under section 10 of the 1998 Act, and “supersession” is to be construed accordingly; and
@ref reg 2 "superseded" (src:34)
GIVEN h IS A `how a decision on an award is changed`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 2: a decision on an award is superseded` h MEANS
    h EQUALS `supersession under section 10 of the 1998 Act`

-- "adult disability payment", "child disability payment", "disability living allowance" and
-- "Scottish adult disability living allowance" are defined by reference to other instruments
-- (the Scottish regulations of 2022, 2021 and 2025, and section 71 of the Social Security
-- Contributions and Benefits Act 1992). They are the constructors of `the benefit paid under
-- an earlier award` in pip-nouns.l4; whether a given award is of one of them is a fact.
-- out of text: Disability Assistance for Working Age People (Scotland) Regulations 2022 reg 2;
-- Disability Assistance for Children and Young People (Scotland) Regulations 2021 reg 2;
-- Disability Assistance (Scottish Adult Disability Living Allowance) Regulations 2025 reg 2;
-- Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 s 71
-- src:17 | “adult disability payment” has the meaning given in regulation 2 of the Disability Assistance for Working Age People (Scotland) Regulations 2022;
@ref reg 2 "adult disability payment" (src:17)
GIVEN b IS A `the benefit paid under an earlier award`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 2: this benefit is adult disability payment` b MEANS
    b EQUALS `adult disability payment`

-- src:23 | “child disability payment” has the meaning given in regulation 2 of the Disability Assistance for Children and Young People (Scotland) Regulations 2021;
@ref reg 2 "child disability payment" (src:23)
GIVEN b IS A `the benefit paid under an earlier award`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 2: this benefit is child disability payment` b MEANS
    b EQUALS `child disability payment`

-- src:26 | “disability living allowance” means disability living allowance under section 71 of the Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992;
@ref reg 2 "disability living allowance" (src:26)
GIVEN b IS A `the benefit paid under an earlier award`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 2: this benefit is disability living allowance` b MEANS
    b EQUALS `disability living allowance`

-- src:33 | “Scottish adult disability living allowance” has the meaning given in regulation 2 of the Disability Assistance (Scottish Adult Disability Living Allowance) Regulations 2025;
@ref reg 2 "Scottish adult disability living allowance" (src:33)
GIVEN b IS A `the benefit paid under an earlier award`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 2: this benefit is Scottish adult disability living allowance` b MEANS
    b EQUALS `Scottish adult disability living allowance`
